cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this software when using the formalization, and cite the upstream
  libraries separately where appropriate. This is a candidate for review;
  publication and external human review are not claimed.
type: software
title: "IP = PSPACE in Lean"
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Troy
version: 0.1.0-review.2
repository-code: "https://github.com/troyjlee/tcs-formalizations"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of Shamir's theorem using Complexitylib's unchanged
  definitions of IP and PSPACE. The hard inclusion combines a uniform
  polynomial-time machine-to-QBF reduction, a certified algebraic interactive
  verifier, and closure of IP under polynomial-time reductions. The reverse
  inclusion is imported from Complexitylib. Developed with Codex assistance;
  original attribution is preserved for all vendored sources. This component
  is being integrated into the TCS formalizations repository.
keywords:
  - computational complexity
  - interactive proofs
  - formal verification
  - Lean
  - PSPACE
